From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 22:31:56 +0200
Subject: leds: lgm-sso: use the macro parameter in GET_SRC_OFFSET()

GET_SRC_OFFSET(pinc) takes a parameter named pinc and then multiplies
pin, so it silently picks up whatever local is called pin at the
expansion site. Its only caller is sso_led_freq_set(), which has such a
local: the pin number it was passed. The argument the call site actually
supplies, off, is dropped.

The two are not the same number. off comes from sso_led_pin_blink_off()
and is relative to the pin's group -- 0..4 for pins 24..28, 0..2 for
pins 29..31, each group having its own LED_BLINK_H8_* register -- while
pin is absolute. The blink registers give every pin six bits: the FPID
rank at off * 6, the GPTC rank at off * 6 + 2, and the two-bit
clock-source select at off * 6 + 4. GET_FREQ_OFFSET() uses its
parameters and lands on the first two correctly. GET_SRC_OFFSET()
computes pin * 6 + 4, which is 148 through 172 for the pins of group 1
and 178 through 190 for group 2, instead of the 4 through 28 the
register has room for. GENMASK(high, low) and the freq_src << high that
follows are then evaluated with shift counts past the width of the type,
and the field the write was meant for is never touched.

So the select that decides whether the hardware reads the pin's FPID
rank or its GPTC rank is never written. The shift counts are undefined
behaviour; where they wrap modulo the width of the type, as they do on
MIPS, the mask and the value land on some other pin's bits in the same
register instead. Pins 0..23 are unaffected, because sso_led_freq_set()
returns early for group 0, and that is also how this survived: no device
tree in tree drives a pin in either of the upper two groups.

Bringing the write back inside the register is not on its own enough to
make a GPTC-derived rate selectable. The same function masks and shifts
both of these fields as though they were three bits wide, which a later
patch in this series fixes -- but that fix has nothing to correct until
the write lands in the register at all.

Fixes: c3987cd2bca3 ("leds: lgm: Add LED controller driver for LGM SoC")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c b/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c
index f66b7366a816..71db8c56d88d 100644
--- a/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@
 #define LED_BLINK_H8_0			0x0
 #define LED_BLINK_H8_1			0x4
 #define GET_FREQ_OFFSET(pin, src)	(((pin) * 6) + ((src) * 2))
-#define GET_SRC_OFFSET(pinc)		(((pin) * 6) + 4)
+#define GET_SRC_OFFSET(pinc)		(((pinc) * 6) + 4)
 
 #define DUTY_CYCLE(x)			(0x8 + ((x) * 4))
 #define SSO_CON0			0x2B0
